==Appendix== === Background Information === * With organizations like ''Bothered About Dungeons & Dragons'' still a powerful force in the early 90s, 1989's AD&D 2nd Edition had done away with previous references to demons, devils, Greek daemons, and Vancian demodands. Two years later, they made a return in this supplement with new "mom-friendly" names. This both helped bring back classic D&D monsters, and helped separate them from their namesakes, allowing for AD&D to create their own mythology. Starting with the [[Blood War]], which also appears here, a decision which would pave the way for ''[[Planescape]]'' in a few years' time. This product is the first to introduce:<ref name="saph">[https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/16892/MC8-Monstrous-Compendium-Outer-Planes-Appendix-2e Shannon Appelcline's Product History]</ref> ** ''[[aasimon]]'' as a new umbrella category for upper-planar entities: [[deva]]s, [[planetar]]s, [[solar]]s, and [[agathinon]] ** ''[[baatezu]]'' as the new name for ''devils'', with some individual types of baatezu also getting renamed ** ''[[gehreleth]]s'' as the new name for ''demodands'' ** ''[[tanar'ri]]'' as the new name for ''demons'' ** ''[[yugoloth]]s'' as the new name for ''daemons''
